    {
      "id": "s02",
      "type": "TITLE_CARD",
      "transition": "fade",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Welcome back. Apple's September event ran long, and the iPhone 18 Pro took the front half of it. Today we're going through what genuinely changed since the 17 Pro, and what only looks new. So what are you actually paying a hundred dollars more for?",
      "data": {
        "title": "What changed, and what did not",
        "subtitle": "iPhone 18 Pro against iPhone 17 Pro",
        "atWord": 18
      },
      "durationFrames": 458
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "type": "APPLE_STAGE",
      "transition": "wipe",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Start with the outside, because that's where most write-ups go wrong. That full width camera plateau isn't new. Apple introduced it on the 17 Pro, and the 18 Pro keeps it, along with the same body size, the same six point three inch screen and the same borders. One thing did move: the plateau is about two millimetres deeper, and that room is there for the new camera module.",
      "data": {
        "appleStage": {
          "headline": "The [shape] carried over",
          "kind": "pro-back",
          "caption": "150.0 by 71.9 millimetres, unchanged",
          "premise": "Same body, same screen, same plateau as the iPhone 17 Pro. Only the depth changed.",
          "color": "blue",
          "cells": [
            {
              "label": "Camera plateau",
              "text": "plateau",
              "sub": "introduced on the 17 Pro",
              "atWord": 11
            },
            {
              "label": "Same body",
              "text": "body",
              "sub": "150.0 x 71.9 mm",
              "atWord": 28
            },
            {
              "label": "About 2 mm deeper",
              "text": "lens",
              "sub": "room for the new module",
              "atWord": 43
            },
            {
              "label": "Same 6.3-inch screen",
              "text": "screen",
              "sub": "and the same borders",
              "atWord": 35
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 686
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "type": "APPLE_STAGE",
      "transition": "fade",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Colour is where the outside did change. Four finishes, and Burgundy is the new one, a deep red reading almost brown indoors. Quieter, and easier to miss: that two tone back is gone, so the rear glass now blends into the frame instead of sitting in a panel. Ceramic Shield covers front and back, which decides whether a bad drop costs you a repair or a shrug.",
      "data": {
        "appleStage": {
          "headline": "Four [finishes], and the two-tone back is gone",
          "kind": "finish-palette",
          "caption": "Burgundy, Glacier, Silver, Black",
          "premise": "The rear glass now blends into the frame. Ceramic Shield front and back.",
          "color": "purple",
          "cells": [
            {
              "label": "Burgundy",
              "sub": "#2a1618,#a16974",
              "text": "finish",
              "atWord": 9
            },
            {
              "label": "Glacier",
              "sub": "#2c3238,#f8fbff",
              "text": "finish",
              "atWord": 5
            },
            {
              "label": "Silver",
              "sub": "#3a3d40,#fdfdfd",
              "text": "finish",
              "atWord": 7
            },
            {
              "label": "Black",
              "sub": "#141414,#c0c0c0",
              "text": "finish",
              "atWord": 8
            }
